  "Question": "If \\(i^2=-1,\\) then \\[ \\left(i-i^{-1}\\right)^{-1}= \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(-2i\\)",
    "C": "\\(2i\\)",
    "D": "\\(-\\frac{i}{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac{i}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "An exponent of \\(-1\\) means reciprocal. Since \\(i^2=-1\\), we have \\(i\\ne0\\), and\n\\[\ni(-i)=-i^2=1.\n\\]\nThus \\(i^{-1}=-i\\), making the inner difference \\(i-(-i)=2i\\), which is also nonzero. To take its reciprocal, multiply numerator and denominator by \\(-i\\):\n\\[\n\\left(i-i^{-1}\\right)^{-1}\n=\\frac{1}{2i}\n=\\frac{-i}{-2i^2}\n=-\\frac{i}{2}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{i}{2}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
